<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      SECURITY MODEL (see SECURITY.md):
      Sandbox is OFF because Grux needs ScreenCaptureKit, AppleEvents,
      and raw mic access across arbitrary apps. OS-level path allowlisting
      is therefore NOT AVAILABLE. The filesystem security boundary lives
      in Swift (FilesystemTool.swift), the ONLY path from Claude to disk.
      That tool enforces:
        • Allowlist of read-only project roots
        • Denylist of .ssh / .aws / .env / Keychain / Mail / Messages / browser profiles
        • 1 MB size cap, binary-file rejection
        • 10 reads/min rate limit
        • Audit log to ~/Library/Application Support/Grux/fs-audit.log
        • Secret-pattern scan on file content before returning
      API keys live in macOS Keychain (service com.gruxai.grux), never on disk.
      Hardened runtime ON. Optional Apple notarization via GRUX_NOTARIZE=1.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <false/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      audio-input + microphone entitlements ARE required for hardened-runtime
      apps (independent of sandbox): without them, AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess
      returns false without even surfacing the TCC prompt. Empirically verified
      2026-04-24 when temporarily removing these caused "ambient: mic not
      authorized" to appear immediately with no user-visible dialog.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.microphone</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      network.server is required for NWListener to accept inbound TCP
      connections from the Grux Phone iOS companion. Pairs with
      NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription + NSBonjourServices (_grux-phone._tcp)
      in Info.plist. Traffic is HMAC-authed and never leaves the user's LAN.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      Personal-information entitlements are hardened-runtime resource-access
      keys (independent of sandbox, same story as audio-input above).
      calendars covers EventKit reads/writes for the Calendar tab and
      calendar tools; addressbook covers CNContactStore for the Contacts
      tab and lookup_contact / create_contact tools. Without them the TCC
      prompt never surfaces and access is silently denied.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      MusicKit NOTE (PROVEN DEAD END 2026-06-19, do NOT retry the profile route):
      `com.apple.developer.musickit` is a RESTRICTED entitlement. On macOS,
      catalog playback via MusicKit/ApplicationMusicPlayer is NOT achievable for
      Grux under its current (non-App-Store, Apple-Development-signed) build. We
      went the full distance and tested every combination on the real signed app:
        - entitlement WITHOUT a provisioning profile  -> macOS kills the app on launch.
        - a Mac Development profile (App ID com.gruxai.grux WITH MusicKit enabled
          under "App Services") WITHOUT the entitlement -> app launches, but
          MusicAuthorization is auto-.denied with no prompt (framework refuses).
        - entitlement WITH that profile embedded       -> still killed on launch,
          because MusicKit is an App SERVICE and Apple does NOT inject the
          musickit entitlement into a Development profile, so it stays
          unauthorized.
      Net: the only way to authorize this entitlement is App Store / TestFlight
      distribution (which provisions it). It cannot be done via the dev-cert +
      profile flow build.sh uses. The App ID, device, and MusicKit capability are
      already registered in the portal as groundwork IF Grux ever ships via the
      App Store. Until then the entitlement is OMITTED (keeps the app launching +
      TCC-stable). Music plays via the AppleScript path: owned-library tracks
      exact + in the background (no skip), catalog tracks via the focus-restored
      path. The gated MusicKitPlayer code stays for the App Store future.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
